## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical skills in cross-DC coordination, configuration management, and state synchronization using Docker Config and Redis Pub/Sub. It also covers rate limiting and error handling under load.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for storing per-tenant quota limits
- Redis PUB/SUB for cross-DC quota propagation
- Quota checks with eventual consistency across peers
- TLS edge routing with Traefik

## Code Example
```javascript
const quota = getQuota(tenantId);
if (quota <= 0) throw new Error('Quota exceeded');

await performImport(data);
decrementQuota(tenantId);
publishQuotaUpdate(tenantId, getQuota(tenantId));
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of per-tenant routing, docker configs, and zero-downtime reconfiguration in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Traefik dynamic config and weighted routing
- Docker Configs for per-tenant policy
- TLS termination at edge proxy
- Multi-DC docker-dca deployment basics
- Observability of per-tenant routing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Traefik dynamic config snippet (example)
{
  "http": {
    "routers": {
      "tenant-ab": {
        "rule": "Host(`api.local`)",
        "tls": { "certResolver": "myresolver" },
        "service": "ab-backend"
      }
    },
    "services": {
      "ab-backend": {
        "loadBalancer": {
          "weighted": {
            "services": [
              { "name": "api-v1", "weight": 80 },
              { "name": "api-v2", "weight": 20 }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

